From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: recover a wsc_m2_sent radio during topo-sync instead of blocking

A 6 GHz radio whose operational-BSS SSID transiently fails is_ssid_match on a
freshly-seeded controller (NetworkSSIDList not yet loaded) is flagged ssid_mismatch,
AutoConfig-Renewed, and regresses to em_state_ctrl_wsc_m2_sent. The topo-sync gate
needs every radio of an AL in topo_sync_pending, so one lagging radio blocks the whole
AL's topology sync forever (no Topology Query -> BSSList/STAList never populate).
Upstream only recovers this in the em_config orch path, not running post-onboarding.
Recover it here too so the mesh self-heals without a manual re-onboard.
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -6124,6 +6172,19 @@ void em_configuration_t::process_ctrl_state()
             {
                 for (auto &em : em_radios) {
                     if (em->get_state() != em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending) {
+                        if (em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_wsc_m2_sent) {
+                            // meta-cmf-bananapi-vcpe: recover from the known second-M1/M2 regression
+                            // here, not only in the em_config orch path (see em_orch_ctrl.cpp). A 6 GHz
+                            // radio whose operational-BSS SSID transiently fails is_ssid_match on a
+                            // freshly-seeded controller (NetworkSSIDList not yet loaded) is flagged
+                            // ssid_mismatch, gets AutoConfig-Renewed, and regresses to wsc_m2_sent.
+                            // Without this, one lagging radio leaves the whole AL out of topo_sync
+                            // forever -> no Topology Query -> BSSList/STAList never populate.
+                            em_printfout("radio %s stuck in wsc_m2_sent -- recovering to topo_sync_pending",
+                                util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
+                            em->set_state(em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending);
+                            continue;
+                        }
                         em_printfout("radio %s is in state:%d, not in topo sync pending state, ignoring",
                             util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str(), em->get_state());
                         em_radios.clear();
